@startuml
title Backstage and document tabs — launch → open → switch → save → close

actor "User" as user
participant "App.tsx" as app
participant "Backstage\n(ui/Backstage)" as backstage
participant "TabStrip / FileMenu" as strip
participant "tabStore\n(recovery/tabs)" as store
participant "Ketcher\n(single editor)" as ketcher
participant "Tauri fs plugin" as fs
participant "localStorage" as ls

== Launch ==
app -> app: render the backstage from the first frame
app -> store: readTabSet() -> index.json, each tab's .json and .ket
store --> app: tabs, names, paths, dirty flags, activeId
app -> ketcher: mount the one editor and restore the active tab
note right of app
  Readiness never dismisses the backstage.
  A missing or corrupt snapshot drops that tab.
end note

== Start a document from Welcome ==
user -> backstage: choose Blank canvas / a template / Open… / Import…
alt Blank canvas
  app -> app: reuse an untouched tab, otherwise create one
  app -> ketcher: load the empty structure (loading flag set)
else Template card
  app -> app: create a new tab with path = null, dirty = true
  app -> ketcher: setMolecule(entry.ket) behind the loading flag
else Open… (.ket)
  app -> app: guard path uniqueness; activate an existing tab instead
  app -> fs: readTextFile(path)
  fs --> app: .ket text
  app -> ketcher: setMolecule(text) behind the loading flag
  app -> app: tab = { path, name: base(path), dirty: false }
  app -> ls: record the recent path
else Import… (mol/smi/inchi/sdf/rxn)
  app -> fs: readTextFile(path)
  fs --> app: structure text
  app -> ketcher: setMolecule(text) behind the loading flag
  app -> app: tab = { path: null, name: base(file), dirty: false }
end
app -> store: write the target tab's clean snapshot and index.json
app -> backstage: close the overlay
backstage --> user: the editor keeps the active tab and canvas

== Switch tabs (one editor) ==
user -> strip: choose another tab
strip -> app: activateTabById(id)
app -> ketcher: getKet() for the outgoing tab
app -> store: flush the outgoing tab snapshot (metadata last)
app -> ketcher: setMolecule(incoming.ket) behind the loading flag
note right of ketcher
  Change events during the load are ignored,
  so the incoming tab stays clean.
end note

== Save / Export ==
user -> strip: File → Save (Ctrl+S) or Save As… (Ctrl+Shift+S)
strip -> app: run the command on the active tab
alt untitled tab
  app -> fs: show the save dialog prefilled <name>.ket
  fs --> app: chosen .ket path
end
app -> ketcher: getKet()
app -> fs: write the .ket text
app -> app: dirty = false; adopt the path on Save As
app -> store: rewrite the tab's clean snapshot
app -> ls: record the recent path
note right of app
  Export never touches path or format;
  it writes a separate Molfile/SMILES/InChI/SVG/PNG file.
end note

== Close ==
user -> app: close the window or one tab
alt no dirty tab
  app -> ketcher: allow the close
else one dirty active tab
  app -> user: Save / Discard / Cancel
  user -> app: Save As cancelled
  app --> user: abort the close
else one dirty inactive tab, or several dirty tabs
  app -> user: Discard / Cancel only
end
opt Discard
  app -> store: delete the dirty tabs' snapshots and rewrite index.json
  app -> ketcher: window.destroy()
end

== Model setup is not replaced ==
user -> backstage: Models rail entry
backstage -> app: onOpenModels()
app -> app: open the real ModelSetupDialog above the overlay
note right of app
  The real Models toolbar entry and dialog remain the model setup
  surface. The rail never shows a fake model list (ADR 0009, 0010).
  The backstage stays behind the dialog and returns when it closes.
end note

== One command path ==
note right of app
  The File menu and the Ketcher toolbar (Save, New, Export, Models)
  dispatch the same active-tab commands. Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Shift+S, Ctrl+O,
  Ctrl+N, Ctrl+W, Ctrl+T and Ctrl+Tab are capture-phase and never
  reach Ketcher; dialogs and the backstage consume the command.
end note

@enduml
